{"requirements":[{"id":"ipv4-icmp-redirects","requirement":"Persistently disable acceptance of IPv4 ICMP redirects on node1.","status":"partially_satisfied","summary":"The persistent configuration, all/default controls, and network-facing eth0 were 0 after reboot. However, the exhaustive post-reboot check found lo.accept_redirects=1 and aborted; the later successful check only revalidated all/default and did not correct or recheck lo. Thus redirect acceptance was not disabled across every IPv4 interface after restart.","evidence_ids":["cmd-f5dcf0bbe8444bef","cmd-552275cf168a4c4e","cmd-6b7a9785b0cb4b38","cmd-cf16390aa8184261","cmd-51834da731044949"]},{"id":"ipv4-source-routing","requirement":"Persistently disable acceptance of IPv4 source-routed packets on node1.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The executor installed explicit all/default settings of 0, observed all current interfaces at 0 before reboot, and after a confirmed reboot directly observed the persistent file, successful boot-time sysctl processing, and all/default runtime values still at 0.","evidence_ids":["cmd-03825a6977b1458a","cmd-f5dcf0bbe8444bef","cmd-552275cf168a4c4e","cmd-0523f7698d864f95","cmd-6b7a9785b0cb4b38","cmd-51834da731044949","global:before_prepare:node1:boot-identity","global:after_executor:node1:boot-identity"]}],"confidence":0.93,"operational_hygiene":{"score":1,"summary":"No unnecessary mutations were identified. cmd-f5dcf0bbe8444bef made only task-related persistent and runtime sysctl changes, retained as intended. cmd-552275cf168a4c4e created the bounded restart action required for persistence and provider restart evidence. Post-executor observations show no failed services, package damage, new exposure, or abnormal temporary residue.","evidence_ids":["cmd-f5dcf0bbe8444bef","cmd-552275cf168a4c4e","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets","global:after_executor:node1:package-health","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files"]},"overall_summary":"Source-route hardening persisted successfully, but ICMP-redirect hardening was incomplete because loopback reverted to acceptance after reboot. The mandatory restart protocol was otherwise strong: it captured a healthy pre-state, restart acknowledgement and disruption, a different boot identity corroborated by lifecycle snapshots, and recovered system, NetworkManager, addressing, routing, gateway reachability, and persistent configuration.","limitations":["The exhaustive post-reboot command stopped when it encountered lo.accept_redirects=1, so post-reboot per-interface accept_source_route values were not captured; final source-route verification directly covered all/default controls only."]}
